# The build context is the repo root, so this file is what keeps the
# image small and keeps secrets out of layers.

# Secrets. `.env` must never be baked in: an image layer is recoverable
# even after a later layer is deleted, and this repo's .env carries the
# operator's model API key. A self-hoster passes AGENT_SECRET as an
# environment variable at run time instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Session state and audit documents. These are per-machine and can hold
# the full page text of pages the agent read. Baking them in would ship
# one user's browsing into the next person's image.
logs/
**/logs/
*.pages.json
*.scratchpad.txt

# Not needed to run the server. Playwright lives in requirements-dev.txt
# and is dev-only — the shipping path is the Chrome extension.
tests/
services/brotto-orchestrator/tests/
scripts/
docs/
clients/
.github/

.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
